1
00:00:00,414 --> 00:00:01,714
(Episode 24)

2
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:15,224
Thank you so much, Ms. Joo.

3
00:00:25,164 --> 00:00:26,774
Are you going back to the office?

4
00:00:28,134 --> 00:00:29,134
Yes.

5
00:00:29,874 --> 00:00:32,304
Then, let's take my car.

6
00:00:33,674 --> 00:00:34,714
Thank you.

7
00:00:37,944 --> 00:00:40,684
So Director Joo was your mother's classmate?

8
00:00:41,614 --> 00:00:46,324
Yes, and not just any classmate. I think they were pretty close.

9
00:00:47,254 --> 00:00:50,124
The story didn't hit the news until after the Manager Na incident.

10
00:00:50,824 --> 00:00:54,234
Ms. Joo must've heard about your mother then.

11
00:00:55,034 --> 00:00:56,564
My mom loved poetry.

12
00:00:57,304 --> 00:00:59,164
She used to recite poems to me before bed.

13
00:01:00,404 --> 00:01:04,274
Ms. Joo knew how she liked spring days and poems too.

14
00:01:06,004 --> 00:01:07,474
Thanks to the Manager Na case,

15
00:01:07,544 --> 00:01:09,414
you found one of your mother's friends,

16
00:01:10,344 --> 00:01:11,784
so I guess some good came out of it.

17
00:01:14,514 --> 00:01:16,724
So, Director Joo...

18
00:01:16,784 --> 00:01:18,924
You said she's one of the Chairman's confidants, right?

19
00:01:19,784 --> 00:01:22,954
Yes. They've been working together for a long time,

20
00:01:23,564 --> 00:01:26,124
and it seems the Chairman trusts and relies on her a lot.

21
00:01:27,634 --> 00:01:30,364
She seems to handle not only company business,

22
00:01:30,434 --> 00:01:31,634
but even private family matters as well.

23
00:01:32,434 --> 00:01:34,274
Oh, I see.

24
00:01:36,004 --> 00:01:39,404
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

25
00:01:40,644 --> 00:01:41,944
Ko Eun Seol...

26
00:01:42,544 --> 00:01:43,644
If I keep her at a distance,

27
00:01:44,414 --> 00:01:46,214
she's the type to stab me in the back.

28
00:01:48,084 --> 00:01:49,853
I need to keep her close by my side...

29
00:01:49,854 --> 00:01:52,224
and keep her on a leash to tame her.

30
00:01:54,924 --> 00:01:56,624
But how am I going to do that?

31
00:02:02,834 --> 00:02:04,304
Goodness, Eun Seol.

32
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:07,034
Hello, ma'am.

33
00:02:11,074 --> 00:02:13,074
You're working late.

34
00:02:13,774 --> 00:02:16,144
The design competition is coming up soon, isn't it?

35
00:02:16,844 --> 00:02:18,444
How's your work coming along?

36
00:02:18,544 --> 00:02:21,254
It's slow going, but I'm doing my best.

37
00:02:22,254 --> 00:02:24,224
Through this competition,

38
00:02:24,554 --> 00:02:26,754
I want to see the future of our Cheongma Group.

39
00:02:30,664 --> 00:02:32,124
And that future?

40
00:02:33,394 --> 00:02:35,134
I want someone like you, Eun Seol,

41
00:02:35,694 --> 00:02:37,334
who has overcome hardship and adversity,

42
00:02:38,234 --> 00:02:40,334
to be the one to prove it.

43
00:02:42,104 --> 00:02:43,104
All right.

44
00:02:43,974 --> 00:02:45,304
I'll do my very best.

45
00:02:50,984 --> 00:02:54,654
Director Joo, I think I might've put too much pressure on her.

46
00:02:55,514 --> 00:02:56,514
Not at all.

47
00:02:56,724 --> 00:02:59,954
I'm sure your message got through to Eun Seol.

48
00:03:03,154 --> 00:03:05,524
All right, then. Keep up the good work.

49
00:03:06,464 --> 00:03:07,464
Sure.

50
00:03:16,174 --> 00:03:17,174
Ma'am.

51
00:03:18,144 --> 00:03:19,144
Yes?

52
00:03:19,145 --> 00:03:20,714
The future of Cheongma you spoke of,

53
00:03:22,044 --> 00:03:23,844
I'll be the one to prove it.

54
00:03:46,064 --> 00:03:47,134
I'm home.

55
00:03:47,674 --> 00:03:49,034
You're home, Mr. Seok Jin?

56
00:03:53,144 --> 00:03:54,914
Did you make all of these by yourself?

57
00:03:55,244 --> 00:03:56,244
Yes.

58
00:03:56,314 --> 00:03:59,014
I'm going to give them all to that nice lady.

59
00:04:00,184 --> 00:04:02,254
But isn't this too much?

60
00:04:03,054 --> 00:04:05,724
What do you mean, too much? Look.

61
00:04:05,824 --> 00:04:08,994
I made them in different colours for each day of the week.

62
00:04:09,294 --> 00:04:11,794
Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday,

63
00:04:11,994 --> 00:04:13,364
Friday, Saturday, and Sunday.

64
00:04:15,794 --> 00:04:16,804
These...

65
00:04:18,304 --> 00:04:21,574
Can you give them to that nice lady?

66
00:04:22,604 --> 00:04:24,004
I can give them to her,

67
00:04:24,844 --> 00:04:27,014
but I think this might be too much for her.

68
00:04:27,374 --> 00:04:28,374
No, it's not.

69
00:04:29,174 --> 00:04:32,944
That kind lady received the keyring I gave her as a gift,

70
00:04:33,214 --> 00:04:34,814
and she really liked it.

71
00:04:35,214 --> 00:04:37,584
So, please make sure you give these to her.

72
00:04:37,984 --> 00:04:38,984
Okay?

73
00:04:46,024 --> 00:04:47,294
I'm home.

74
00:04:47,394 --> 00:04:48,594
You're late.

75
00:04:48,734 --> 00:04:50,904
You must be busy with the design competition.

76
00:04:51,834 --> 00:04:54,134
No, it's not that.

77
00:04:55,504 --> 00:04:57,774
Director Joo. Let's talk in my room.

78
00:05:06,784 --> 00:05:09,114
Of all people, Ko Eun Seol just had to show up then.

79
00:05:09,184 --> 00:05:11,124
Right when Ms. Park was in danger.

80
00:05:11,454 --> 00:05:13,554
You should've seen how much she admired Ko Eun Seol.

81
00:05:13,624 --> 00:05:14,994
It's so annoying.

82
00:05:16,194 --> 00:05:17,194
So?

83
00:05:17,424 --> 00:05:19,564
The four of you had a meal together?

84
00:05:20,464 --> 00:05:24,804
Yes. But even then, being so clueless and infuriating,

85
00:05:24,864 --> 00:05:27,304
Ms. Park kept piling meat onto Ko Eun Seol's plate,

86
00:05:27,404 --> 00:05:29,604
and Ko Eun Seol just gobbled it all up.

87
00:05:30,974 --> 00:05:32,744
It was disgusting to watch.

88
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:33,914
So...

89
00:05:34,414 --> 00:05:36,014
what do you want my help with?

90
00:05:37,244 --> 00:05:38,314
You told me before...

91
00:05:38,384 --> 00:05:39,844
to trust you with everything.

92
00:05:40,814 --> 00:05:44,054
Isn't there a way to handle Ms. Park?

93
00:05:46,754 --> 00:05:47,754
All right.

94
00:05:48,624 --> 00:05:51,064
You just focus on your work.

95
00:05:51,794 --> 00:05:53,964
You have to win this signature line yourself.

96
00:05:54,034 --> 00:05:56,064
That's how you can show Ko Eun Seol up.

97
00:05:56,464 --> 00:05:59,064
Only then can you become the main face of Cheongma.

98
00:06:00,504 --> 00:06:01,704
Don't worry.

99
00:06:01,804 --> 00:06:03,744
I can easily beat someone like Ko Eun Seol.

100
00:06:08,274 --> 00:06:11,284
The internal design competition is coming up soon, right?

101
00:06:11,444 --> 00:06:14,414
Everyone seems so preoccupied with it lately.

102
00:06:14,814 --> 00:06:17,324
Why don't you show some generous support...

103
00:06:17,384 --> 00:06:19,284
to encourage them?

104
00:06:19,584 --> 00:06:21,254
Yes, of course.

105
00:06:22,054 --> 00:06:23,664
Hae Ra, is there anything you need?

106
00:06:24,294 --> 00:06:25,294
Really?

107
00:06:25,864 --> 00:06:28,694
Then throw a huge party to celebrate after the competition.

108
00:06:28,764 --> 00:06:29,834
A company-sponsored one.

109
00:06:31,034 --> 00:06:32,434
A party?

110
00:06:32,864 --> 00:06:34,134
Well, it makes sense.

111
00:06:34,634 --> 00:06:36,203
We're deciding the signature line...

112
00:06:36,204 --> 00:06:38,974
for the first new brand Cheongma has launched in years.

113
00:06:39,044 --> 00:06:40,214
That's the least you can do.

114
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:42,044
You know, that's not a bad idea.

115
00:06:42,114 --> 00:06:44,744
It'd be great for publicity. Right?

116
00:06:45,044 --> 00:06:48,654
Director Joo, why don't you handle that?

117
00:06:48,714 --> 00:06:52,284
Sure, I'll plan a launch gala for Shoejoy.

118
00:06:53,354 --> 00:06:56,224
The signature line will be my design anyway.

119
00:06:57,724 --> 00:07:00,264
I should decide on a dress code.

120
00:07:02,064 --> 00:07:04,664
It's not good to be so overconfident.

121
00:07:05,164 --> 00:07:07,474
You need to stay on your toes until the very end.

122
00:07:08,934 --> 00:07:12,574
It seems Ko Eun Seol is also preparing diligently.

123
00:07:13,374 --> 00:07:16,374
No matter what she tries, she's still beneath my feet.

124
00:07:18,544 --> 00:07:20,584
But Mom, why are you always so neutral?

125
00:07:22,554 --> 00:07:23,554
Am I?

126
00:07:23,654 --> 00:07:26,954
I mean, most moms think their own daughter is the best.

127
00:07:27,354 --> 00:07:28,724
It's not like that.

128
00:07:28,994 --> 00:07:30,994
A woman like Eun Seol, who endured ten years...

129
00:07:31,064 --> 00:07:32,464
after being falsely accused,

130
00:07:32,594 --> 00:07:34,934
isn't an easy opponent.

131
00:07:36,764 --> 00:07:39,734
I'm so sick of people talking about Ko Eun Seol everywhere I go.

132
00:07:40,064 --> 00:07:41,704
Do you have to add to that, Mom?

133
00:07:42,604 --> 00:07:43,604
I only meant...

134
00:07:43,674 --> 00:07:44,844
Hae Ra, wait.

135
00:07:46,204 --> 00:07:50,514
I can't believe you. Try to see it from her perspective.

136
00:07:50,684 --> 00:07:54,214
At the office, maybe. But at home, you're her mom.

137
00:07:56,154 --> 00:07:57,384
All right.

138
00:08:02,054 --> 00:08:04,524
What lovely sunshine.

139
00:08:10,904 --> 00:08:13,004
I thought you had a dryer.

140
00:08:13,304 --> 00:08:15,134
Why are you airing out the blankets again?

141
00:08:15,734 --> 00:08:18,144
Even with a dryer, on a nice sunny day like this,

142
00:08:18,204 --> 00:08:20,314
they say it's good to air them out in the sun.

143
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:23,144
Sounds like something a spoiled person would say.

144
00:08:25,484 --> 00:08:28,914
By the way, did you divorce the kid's father?

145
00:08:29,314 --> 00:08:30,824
I doubt you're a widow.

146
00:08:32,124 --> 00:08:33,754
Why do you want to know?

147
00:08:33,824 --> 00:08:36,024
Does there have to be a reason to be curious?

148
00:08:36,354 --> 00:08:38,224
We're neighbours,

149
00:08:38,324 --> 00:08:40,764
so getting to know that much is just part of being neighbourly.

150
00:08:40,964 --> 00:08:43,534
That's not being neighbourly. That's being rude.

151
00:08:43,664 --> 00:08:45,134
Rude? Please.

152
00:08:45,264 --> 00:08:47,904
Back in my day, we even knew how many spoons...

153
00:08:47,974 --> 00:08:49,374
were at our neighbour's table.

154
00:08:50,504 --> 00:08:54,714
Is saying you're divorced or widowed such a terrible thing?

155
00:08:54,774 --> 00:08:56,074
There's no father.

156
00:08:56,144 --> 00:08:58,614
- What? - I said he doesn't exist.

157
00:08:58,684 --> 00:09:00,684
There was never a father to begin with.

158
00:09:00,754 --> 00:09:03,884
- Is that clear? - Oh my, then...

159
00:09:04,184 --> 00:09:05,924
you had him on your own out of wedlock?

160
00:09:05,954 --> 00:09:09,124
Yes, I had him out of wedlock. So?

161
00:09:09,824 --> 00:09:10,964
Right.

162
00:09:11,364 --> 00:09:14,564
No wonder you have no taste in men.

163
00:09:14,594 --> 00:09:15,594
Ma'am!

164
00:09:17,734 --> 00:09:21,804
Prying into someone's past like that is a form of harassment.

165
00:09:24,904 --> 00:09:26,404
Harassment? Please.

166
00:09:26,474 --> 00:09:29,074
Did I hit you or something?

167
00:09:29,374 --> 00:09:32,514
Unbelievable. No wonder she's without a husband.

168
00:09:38,484 --> 00:09:39,554
I'm off.

169
00:09:39,654 --> 00:09:40,654
Where are you going?

170
00:09:41,224 --> 00:09:42,754
Did you get a job?

171
00:09:43,894 --> 00:09:44,894
No.

172
00:09:45,294 --> 00:09:48,364
Then where could you possibly be going at this hour?

173
00:09:49,534 --> 00:09:51,534
This is me practising.

174
00:09:52,064 --> 00:09:53,064
Practising?

175
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:55,004
If I want to get a job someday,

176
00:09:55,074 --> 00:09:57,444
I have to get my body used to a routine.

177
00:09:57,874 --> 00:09:59,474
Nine-to-six, is it?

178
00:10:00,444 --> 00:10:02,214
I guess you could call it commute training.

179
00:10:02,444 --> 00:10:04,484
I'm going to do about 30 laps around the neighbourhood.

180
00:10:04,744 --> 00:10:05,884
I'll be back.

181
00:10:05,944 --> 00:10:07,354
Call me if you need bean sprouts.

182
00:10:10,284 --> 00:10:13,124
To think I went through labour for him.

183
00:10:13,184 --> 00:10:15,694
My goodness.

184
00:10:29,834 --> 00:10:31,044
Seriously?

185
00:10:33,174 --> 00:10:35,214
Ma'am!

186
00:10:36,674 --> 00:10:39,514
(Cheongma)

187
00:10:40,314 --> 00:10:42,854
- What's this? - It's a gift for So Yeon.

188
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:44,554
A gift for Ms. Park?

189
00:10:47,394 --> 00:10:50,224
Are you kidding me? It's so childish.

190
00:10:50,564 --> 00:10:52,524
It might look that way to you,

191
00:10:53,224 --> 00:10:55,634
but So Yeon will absolutely love it.

192
00:10:57,034 --> 00:10:59,434
We just have completely different tastes.

193
00:11:01,034 --> 00:11:05,604
I heard she returned all the gifts you've sent her so far.

194
00:11:05,844 --> 00:11:09,174
I know. She even refused all those nice designer bags.

195
00:11:10,214 --> 00:11:13,014
Don't take what happened this morning too hard.

196
00:11:13,784 --> 00:11:15,454
That's why I'm giving you this.

197
00:11:16,154 --> 00:11:19,724
Chief Cha and So Yeon. Give her this and forget about it for a while.

198
00:11:20,184 --> 00:11:22,724
You should just focus on the upcoming competition.

199
00:11:23,194 --> 00:11:24,194
I will.

200
00:11:24,994 --> 00:11:26,294
Thank you, Director Joo.

201
00:11:27,134 --> 00:11:29,594
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

202
00:11:31,504 --> 00:11:33,834
The competition is closing in. Shouldn't you be at work?

203
00:11:34,404 --> 00:11:36,104
I'm allowed to take a short break.

204
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,404
Besides,

205
00:11:37,474 --> 00:11:39,274
I only get my energy back after seeing you.

206
00:11:43,344 --> 00:11:44,344
What's that?

207
00:11:47,184 --> 00:11:48,754
It's something my mother made.

208
00:11:50,524 --> 00:11:52,184
She made it for Ko Eun Seol, didn't she?

209
00:11:53,584 --> 00:11:54,594
Yes.

210
00:11:56,024 --> 00:11:57,964
What's so special about Ko Eun Seol?

211
00:11:58,824 --> 00:12:00,863
- Hae Ra. - Why is everyone making...

212
00:12:00,864 --> 00:12:02,734
such a big deal out of her?

213
00:12:03,394 --> 00:12:05,604
My mom, you, and even your mom.

214
00:12:07,034 --> 00:12:09,134
Why does she always get attention without even trying?

215
00:12:09,204 --> 00:12:10,674
And from my own people, too.

216
00:12:10,904 --> 00:12:13,004
- Hae Ra, that's not it. - Forget it.

217
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:15,144
You're no different.

218
00:12:15,214 --> 00:12:17,484
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

219
00:12:29,694 --> 00:12:30,964
Where's Ko Eun Seol?

220
00:12:31,894 --> 00:12:34,594
She went to present her proposal to the Chief.

221
00:12:36,934 --> 00:12:38,734
She couldn't even wait until I got back?

222
00:12:45,244 --> 00:12:46,244
Come in.

223
00:12:52,114 --> 00:12:54,454
Here's the design proposal you requested.

224
00:12:54,684 --> 00:12:55,954
Okay, I'll take a look.

225
00:12:56,454 --> 00:12:57,454
By the way,

226
00:12:58,254 --> 00:12:59,423
you know that I'm recusing myself...

227
00:12:59,424 --> 00:13:01,294
from judging this competition, right?

228
00:13:01,654 --> 00:13:03,354
Yes. Since you're the head of the team,

229
00:13:03,424 --> 00:13:05,524
I understand you're only able to attend.

230
00:13:07,764 --> 00:13:09,634
How are your preparations coming along?

231
00:13:10,394 --> 00:13:12,634
I did the best I could within my limits.

232
00:13:13,104 --> 00:13:15,104
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

233
00:13:17,444 --> 00:13:18,674
You're putting that to good use.

234
00:13:20,104 --> 00:13:21,114
This?

235
00:13:21,374 --> 00:13:23,984
I put all of my presentation files on here.

236
00:13:24,244 --> 00:13:27,554
I felt like having this keyring would give me strength.

237
00:13:30,114 --> 00:13:32,624
By the way... Here.

238
00:13:33,554 --> 00:13:35,394
My mother asked me to give this to you.

239
00:13:35,894 --> 00:13:36,994
Really?

240
00:13:40,564 --> 00:13:43,364
Gosh, they're so pretty. Thank you.

241
00:13:59,914 --> 00:14:00,954
Ji Soo.

242
00:14:01,384 --> 00:14:04,254
The overseas samples are in the basement storage, right?

243
00:14:05,184 --> 00:14:08,254
Yes. Last year's samples should be there.

244
00:14:08,824 --> 00:14:10,894
- I'll be right back. - Okay.

245
00:14:25,604 --> 00:14:27,744
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

246
00:15:19,164 --> 00:15:21,964
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

247
00:15:27,574 --> 00:15:29,604
Ms. Kang, aren't you going to lunch?

248
00:15:30,504 --> 00:15:34,214
No, I have a bit of indigestion. You two go ahead.

249
00:15:34,374 --> 00:15:36,814
Okay, we'll get going then.

250
00:15:43,354 --> 00:15:45,484
(How Foot Imbalance Triggers a Chain Reaction)

251
00:15:45,654 --> 00:15:46,724
Ko Eun Seol,

252
00:15:47,254 --> 00:15:49,324
when did you prepare all of this?

253
00:16:03,234 --> 00:16:05,204
You were always like this, even when we were in school.

254
00:16:05,774 --> 00:16:09,514
The things I barely managed to get, you always got so easily.

255
00:16:12,544 --> 00:16:13,584
Hey.

256
00:16:14,184 --> 00:16:15,284
Seok Jin!

257
00:16:36,934 --> 00:16:40,574
(Do Not Block Passageway)

258
00:16:42,844 --> 00:16:44,184
You need to learn...

259
00:16:44,744 --> 00:16:47,384
that you can't just breeze through everything.

260
00:16:48,054 --> 00:16:52,424
Winning the design competition and getting Seok Jin, all of it.

261
00:17:21,084 --> 00:17:23,314
Darn, I didn't bring my phone.

262
00:17:33,294 --> 00:17:34,364
Hello?

263
00:17:35,464 --> 00:17:38,464
Is anyone out there? There's someone in here.

264
00:17:44,304 --> 00:17:45,944
Is anyone out there?

265
00:17:51,114 --> 00:17:52,114
Ko Eun Seol.

266
00:17:52,684 --> 00:17:54,184
You're going to get what's coming to you.

267
00:18:03,554 --> 00:18:06,024
- Boss, I'm going to take this out. - Okay.

268
00:18:11,704 --> 00:18:13,504
Welcome.

269
00:18:14,574 --> 00:18:15,734
One iced Americano.

270
00:18:16,404 --> 00:18:18,344
One iced Americano, correct?

271
00:18:18,374 --> 00:18:19,374
Yes.

272
00:18:21,614 --> 00:18:23,744
I'll have that right out for you.

273
00:18:33,584 --> 00:18:36,794
Sir, here's your iced Americano.

274
00:18:50,234 --> 00:18:52,004
Should I throw that away for you?

275
00:18:52,074 --> 00:18:53,074
A refill.

276
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:56,974
Sir, we don't offer refills here.

277
00:18:58,114 --> 00:19:00,744
Then you shouldn't have packed it with so much ice.

278
00:19:01,184 --> 00:19:02,954
There was barely any coffee,

279
00:19:03,114 --> 00:19:05,184
and the rest was just ice.

280
00:19:05,684 --> 00:19:08,954
Sir, that was the standard amount of coffee and ice.

281
00:19:09,054 --> 00:19:12,163
Just give me what I'm asking for.

282
00:19:12,164 --> 00:19:13,424
You little...

283
00:19:14,864 --> 00:19:16,663
Hey, what are you doing?

284
00:19:16,664 --> 00:19:20,264
Sir, you should've listened the first time.

285
00:19:20,934 --> 00:19:23,304
We don't do refills here.

286
00:19:23,734 --> 00:19:25,104
If that's hard to understand,

287
00:19:25,244 --> 00:19:26,974
maybe I should explain it to you physically.

288
00:19:27,814 --> 00:19:28,814
Sir.

289
00:19:31,214 --> 00:19:35,854
The second I let go of your hand, you will leave immediately.

290
00:19:36,184 --> 00:19:38,623
And you will not come back.

291
00:19:38,624 --> 00:19:40,654
All right. I get it!

292
00:19:48,234 --> 00:19:50,334
Boss, where should I put this?

293
00:19:52,264 --> 00:19:54,674
Over there.

294
00:19:58,774 --> 00:20:00,544
What's wrong with me?

295
00:20:01,644 --> 00:20:02,944
I must be crazy.

296
00:20:08,984 --> 00:20:11,054
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

297
00:20:11,324 --> 00:20:14,024
Where did you get this video?

298
00:20:14,794 --> 00:20:17,424
As you instructed, I was tailing Bae Jong Min,

299
00:20:17,494 --> 00:20:19,894
and I found out a PI was following him as well.

300
00:20:19,964 --> 00:20:22,064
Who hired the private detectives?

301
00:20:22,434 --> 00:20:24,504
It seemed like they were working for the woman,

302
00:20:24,764 --> 00:20:26,234
but I got to them first,

303
00:20:26,364 --> 00:20:28,234
and they've agreed not to release the video.

304
00:20:29,104 --> 00:20:30,304
Are you sure?

305
00:20:31,004 --> 00:20:32,804
I'm asking if you're sure they've been silenced.

306
00:20:33,604 --> 00:20:36,844
Yes. I have it in writing, with a thumbprint signature.

307
00:20:37,014 --> 00:20:38,684
Good work, Director Joo.

308
00:20:40,214 --> 00:20:42,054
Bae Jong Min, that lying punk.

309
00:20:57,634 --> 00:20:58,664
Young Hoon,

310
00:20:59,304 --> 00:21:00,534
I messed up.

311
00:21:01,274 --> 00:21:03,634
Look, she's a TA in my department.

312
00:21:04,134 --> 00:21:06,674
I never meant for this to happen.

313
00:21:07,044 --> 00:21:09,874
You know things are bad with my wife.

314
00:21:10,844 --> 00:21:13,043
I was just looking for comfort...

315
00:21:13,044 --> 00:21:14,114
Shut it.

316
00:21:16,154 --> 00:21:18,224
This video won't get out, right?

317
00:21:18,954 --> 00:21:21,694
If this gets out, my life and career will be over.

318
00:21:22,224 --> 00:21:24,324
Please help me out, Young Hoon.

319
00:21:26,924 --> 00:21:27,964
If this video gets out,

320
00:21:28,034 --> 00:21:29,794
you're not the only one who's finished.

321
00:21:29,894 --> 00:21:32,664
I recommended you for the board, so I'll go down with you.

322
00:21:34,034 --> 00:21:36,604
Young Hoon, I'm begging you this one last time.

323
00:21:39,774 --> 00:21:43,414
Consider yourself lucky that one of my people found it first.

324
00:21:48,584 --> 00:21:50,284
Hello?

325
00:21:51,384 --> 00:21:52,724
Is anyone out there?

326
00:22:00,864 --> 00:22:02,634
The presentation is tomorrow,

327
00:22:02,694 --> 00:22:04,634
and I haven't even finished preparing for it.

328
00:22:06,064 --> 00:22:08,304
What am I going to do?

329
00:22:18,414 --> 00:22:22,314
Ms. Kang, I've fixed the typo on slide four and re-uploaded it.

330
00:22:25,254 --> 00:22:26,824
Ms. Kang?

331
00:22:27,724 --> 00:22:29,354
Yes, what is it?

332
00:22:29,554 --> 00:22:31,694
I'm done fixing the typo in the presentation.

333
00:22:32,024 --> 00:22:33,624
Right. Good work.

334
00:22:41,574 --> 00:22:42,874
Yes, Ms. Joo.

335
00:22:45,844 --> 00:22:49,544
On slide five, there's too much focus on aesthetics.

336
00:22:50,114 --> 00:22:51,444
You need to emphasize the premium quality...

337
00:22:51,514 --> 00:22:53,384
that elevates the wearer's status and class...

338
00:22:53,444 --> 00:22:55,284
the moment they put on the shoes.

339
00:22:58,384 --> 00:22:59,454
Kang Hae Ra.

340
00:23:01,354 --> 00:23:02,354
Yes?

341
00:23:02,724 --> 00:23:06,124
The competition is tomorrow. Where's your head at?

342
00:23:09,434 --> 00:23:12,064
Is something wrong?

343
00:23:15,074 --> 00:23:17,204
Tell me. What is it?

344
00:23:18,344 --> 00:23:19,844
I think I did something foolish.

345
00:23:21,174 --> 00:23:22,544
You did something reckless?

346
00:23:22,844 --> 00:23:25,584
I locked Ko Eun Seol up.

347
00:23:26,944 --> 00:23:28,654
Start making sense.

348
00:23:29,684 --> 00:23:32,454
I couldn't stand seeing Ko Eun Seol act so smugly,

349
00:23:32,724 --> 00:23:34,254
so I locked her in storage.

350
00:23:35,224 --> 00:23:37,024
But I didn't mean to do it.

351
00:23:37,424 --> 00:23:40,264
She just kept getting under my skin.

352
00:23:40,324 --> 00:23:42,164
And everyone only pays attention to her.

353
00:23:43,764 --> 00:23:45,434
What do I do?

354
00:23:46,664 --> 00:23:48,704
If she finds out it was me, she won't let this slide.

355
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:54,614
Ms. Joo, please help me.

356
00:24:01,184 --> 00:24:02,414
Hello?

357
00:24:03,784 --> 00:24:05,724
Is anyone out there?

358
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:09,924
Please, open the door.

359
00:24:18,904 --> 00:24:20,504
Hello?

360
00:24:21,474 --> 00:24:23,404
Is anyone out there?

361
00:24:23,874 --> 00:24:26,704
Someone's in here. Please open the door.

362
00:24:28,914 --> 00:24:29,974
Hello?

363
00:24:30,044 --> 00:24:32,914
Right, Ko Eun Seol. I'll help you.

364
00:24:33,514 --> 00:24:36,084
But not today.

365
00:24:36,714 --> 00:24:38,324
You've waited ten years, haven't you?

366
00:24:39,054 --> 00:24:40,524
Since that's the case, you can wait...

367
00:24:41,054 --> 00:24:42,954
just one more day.

368
00:24:51,404 --> 00:24:53,134
My presentation is tomorrow. What am I going to do?

369
00:24:56,404 --> 00:24:57,774
What if I'm still stuck here tomorrow?

370
00:25:01,874 --> 00:25:02,974
No way.

371
00:25:09,154 --> 00:25:10,414
Come on.

372
00:25:11,114 --> 00:25:12,124
Darn it!

373
00:25:29,174 --> 00:25:31,174
(Cheongma Group's New Brand Shoejoy)

374
00:25:31,234 --> 00:25:33,304
(Signature Line Design Competition)

375
00:25:35,074 --> 00:25:36,944
CEO Kang and Chairman Kim are entering.

376
00:25:51,294 --> 00:25:52,494
(Cheongma Group's New Brand Shoejoy)

377
00:25:53,624 --> 00:25:54,764
All right, everyone, be seated.

378
00:26:03,034 --> 00:26:05,204
We'll now begin the design review...

379
00:26:05,304 --> 00:26:07,944
to determine the first signature line...

380
00:26:08,014 --> 00:26:09,974
for Cheongma's new brand, Shoejoy.

381
00:26:10,614 --> 00:26:13,684
This competition will select the one main design...

382
00:26:13,784 --> 00:26:15,414
that will represent Cheongma's...

383
00:26:15,484 --> 00:26:18,184
future global expansion and its brand identity.

384
00:26:18,654 --> 00:26:20,583
Each participant will have ten minutes...

385
00:26:20,584 --> 00:26:22,354
for their design concept presentation...

386
00:26:22,424 --> 00:26:24,194
followed by a five-minute Q and A session.

387
00:26:24,494 --> 00:26:26,424
The on-site scores from the judges will be combined...

388
00:26:26,494 --> 00:26:28,664
to determine the final selected design.

389
00:26:29,134 --> 00:26:30,764
Now, for our first presentation,

390
00:26:31,034 --> 00:26:34,774
we will begin with Design Team Leader Kang Hae Ra.

391
00:27:20,214 --> 00:27:21,214
Mom?

392
00:27:25,784 --> 00:27:28,624
Eun Seol, are you okay?

393
00:27:40,834 --> 00:27:44,034
We have to go now. It's your turn to present.

394
00:27:44,274 --> 00:27:45,474
Just a moment.

395
00:27:45,844 --> 00:27:48,114
The flash drive with my presentation is gone.

396
00:27:48,474 --> 00:27:49,544
This is terrible.

397
00:27:49,974 --> 00:27:52,344
Eun Seol, you have to get going right now.

398
00:28:00,854 --> 00:28:02,394
The design you see here...

399
00:28:02,624 --> 00:28:04,764
is the noble silhouette, inspired by...

400
00:28:04,824 --> 00:28:07,994
the S-curve of traditional French riding boots.

401
00:28:08,794 --> 00:28:12,264
It elegantly defines the line from the instep to the ankle,

402
00:28:12,864 --> 00:28:14,364
making the leg line appear its longest...

403
00:28:14,504 --> 00:28:17,074
and most graceful with the perfect golden ratio.

404
00:28:18,004 --> 00:28:19,004
Next...

405
00:28:22,174 --> 00:28:23,174
I apologize.

406
00:28:25,084 --> 00:28:27,544
What's this? You're late.

407
00:28:28,884 --> 00:28:30,214
There were extenuating circumstances.

408
00:28:31,114 --> 00:28:32,124
I apologize.

409
00:28:42,964 --> 00:28:47,904
Next is the presentation from the Design Team's Ko Eun Seol.

410
00:28:54,244 --> 00:28:57,414
Due to an incident where she lost her presentation file,

411
00:28:57,514 --> 00:28:59,444
she will be presenting without any visual materials,

412
00:28:59,684 --> 00:29:01,183
using just her sketches.

413
00:29:01,184 --> 00:29:02,484
We appreciate your understanding.

414
00:29:04,854 --> 00:29:06,954
Up until now, we've considered shoes...

415
00:29:07,284 --> 00:29:09,594
to be nothing more than a fashion statement.

416
00:29:10,694 --> 00:29:12,324
Sleek lines,

417
00:29:12,664 --> 00:29:15,864
expensive materials to attract attention...

418
00:29:16,934 --> 00:29:18,504
That's all we've ever focused on.

419
00:29:19,604 --> 00:29:21,934
When it comes to enabling a proper walking gait,

420
00:29:22,304 --> 00:29:25,874
the wearer's foot health has always been an afterthought.

421
00:29:28,144 --> 00:29:31,344
A proper gait is the foundation for the entire body's balance,

422
00:29:31,984 --> 00:29:32,984
starting from the feet.

423
00:29:34,214 --> 00:29:36,053
Instead of treating shoes...

424
00:29:36,054 --> 00:29:38,184
as disposable items or fashion accessories,

425
00:29:38,754 --> 00:29:41,384
- as an extension of the body... - Mr. Seok Jin, help!

426
00:29:41,754 --> 00:29:43,124
I've reassessed their purpose.

427
00:29:49,334 --> 00:29:50,334
Mom, what's wrong?

428
00:29:50,764 --> 00:29:53,504
I don't want to go to the community center today.

429
00:29:54,934 --> 00:29:56,134
Is that why you called?

430
00:29:56,804 --> 00:29:57,804
Yes.

431
00:29:58,304 --> 00:30:00,044
I don't want to go to the community center today.

432
00:30:01,614 --> 00:30:02,774
You can't call me about things like this.

433
00:30:02,874 --> 00:30:04,074
I'm working right now.

434
00:30:04,574 --> 00:30:06,514
Oh, right. I'm sorry.

435
00:30:06,884 --> 00:30:09,684
But this is a big deal to me.

436
00:30:10,484 --> 00:30:12,484
I'm feeling really down today.

437
00:30:13,284 --> 00:30:14,284
All right, fine. Don't go.

438
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:17,224
But make sure you eat properly at home.

439
00:30:18,394 --> 00:30:21,564
Okay. Don't worry, Mr. Seok Jin.

440
00:30:28,134 --> 00:30:29,504
Excuse me, ma'am. Just a moment.

441
00:30:31,204 --> 00:30:32,344
I'm sorry, but that...

442
00:30:33,604 --> 00:30:34,604
Oh, this?

443
00:30:35,274 --> 00:30:36,314
Do you recognise this?

444
00:30:36,974 --> 00:30:40,614
Someone threw it away or lost it, but it was just lying over there.

445
00:30:41,444 --> 00:30:43,214
It looked important, so I picked it up.

446
00:30:43,854 --> 00:30:45,124
I know the owner.

447
00:30:47,924 --> 00:30:48,924
Thank you.

448
00:30:55,094 --> 00:30:58,964
It's engineered to adapt flexibly to every joint's...

449
00:31:00,264 --> 00:31:01,264
movement.

450
00:31:01,674 --> 00:31:02,674
Just a minute.

451
00:31:04,034 --> 00:31:05,044
Let's stop here.

452
00:31:07,144 --> 00:31:08,144
Ko Eun Seol.

453
00:31:09,674 --> 00:31:12,944
While the content of your design matters,

454
00:31:14,914 --> 00:31:17,184
this session also evaluates your fundamental ability...

455
00:31:17,714 --> 00:31:21,354
to prepare and present your work to the public.

456
00:31:24,294 --> 00:31:26,394
The presentation ends here.

457
00:31:27,824 --> 00:31:28,834
Wrap it up.

458
00:31:32,934 --> 00:31:33,934
Just a moment.

459
00:31:47,684 --> 00:31:48,714
Here.

460
00:31:49,614 --> 00:31:52,424
I found Ko Eun Seol's presentation file.

461
00:32:37,534 --> 00:32:41,464
(A Trap Called Desire)

462
00:32:41,634 --> 00:32:44,104
That's always the issue with you.

463
00:32:44,174 --> 00:32:47,744
I'm not just her mother, I'm also Hae Ra's boss.

464
00:32:48,074 --> 00:32:51,344
Seok Jin, you're going to marry me, right?

465
00:32:51,714 --> 00:32:53,244
Who am I to you, Eun Seol?

466
00:32:53,544 --> 00:32:55,854
Not as your lawyer, but as your man.

467
00:32:56,114 --> 00:32:58,054
Would you like to have dinner sometime?

468
00:32:58,314 --> 00:33:00,324
So they're meeting behind my back?

469
00:33:00,584 --> 00:33:04,754
How did you know I was there that day?

470
00:33:04,954 --> 00:33:06,324
Yes, the 500,000 dollars!

471
00:33:06,394 --> 00:33:07,694
I'm going to find Eun Seol's birth mother...

472
00:33:07,764 --> 00:33:10,064
and use the money to back Eun Guk's business.

473
00:33:10,164 --> 00:33:12,764
Do you know where Joo Ae Sook is now?
